Negative-findings notes:

- Moonshot's only published claim is qualitative: coding/agent performance "close to K3" with more efficient thinking vs K2.7 Code (vendor, via KuCoin/PANews). CCTest reporting (2026-09) explicitly notes the near-K3 claim is not yet backed by public benchmarks or independent testing; no LiveCodeBench / SWE-bench third-party scores exist as of 2026-09-29.
- OpenCode's compare data shows no benchmark rows for this model (50/100 neutral placeholders only) and near-zero usage (17 sessions, 0% token share, 2026-09-29).
- Zero verified public benchmark numbers for this exact model/ID → saved as `.md.excluded` per the template's SELF-EXCLUSION rule. Re-research once independent scores (LiveCodeBench, SWE-bench, TB2.1, AA Index) are published.

